  1. The quench channel closes immediately: creating long-wavelength
     medium quanta at the door injects ~9e-84 eV⁴ — about 97
     orders below even the door's own keV budget. Honest and dead.
  2. Every computed channel is keV-class or below. The MeV question
     now rests on exactly TWO live levers, both named, neither
     prejudged: the spherical focusing amplification (a number the
     adaptive run is computing right now), and the Standard-Model
     sector's crossing (task #14 — where most of the bath's energy
     actually lives, and the only channel big enough to matter if
     focusing falls short).
  3. If both levers fail, the honest endpoint is: the reconstruction
     under-funds BBN and says so — that becomes an outer-spec tension
     for the whole build, not a knob to turn.
